      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14186058/assets/29559fd9cbee104e92c719d4c33dd7560d2e2ab8c4f25490659b73f07350debc.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ in the figure above given that $\\angle AOC$ is complementary to $\\angle COD.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we have \n\n$$\nm\\angle AOC=x + 24^{\\circ}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nm\\angle COD=3x.\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince $\\angle AOC$ is complementary to $\\angle COD,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+{24}^{∘})+3x & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 4x+{24}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={66}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={16.5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
